sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant A as Other app
    participant T as TUN (VpnService)
    participant E as Engine (netstack)
    participant D as Fake-IP DNS
    participant P as Adapter (SOCKS5/HTTP[/TLS])
    participant X as Proxy
    participant S as Destination
    A->>T: DNS A? example.com (UDP/53, any resolver)
    T->>E: UDP packet
    E->>D: query
    D-->>A: A 198.18.4.7 (TTL 5 s) — never leaves the phone
    A->>T: TCP SYN to 198.18.4.7:443
    T->>E: SYN (not answered yet)
    E->>D: reverse 198.18.4.7 → example.com
    E->>P: Dial(example.com:443)
    P->>X: TCP (+TLS) to proxy, protected socket
    P->>X: SOCKS5 CONNECT example.com:443 / HTTP CONNECT example.com:443
    X->>S: proxy resolves and connects
    X-->>P: success
    P-->>E: tunnel ready
    E-->>A: SYN-ACK (handshake completes only now)
    A->>S: app bytes ⇄ relayed through the tunnel
    Note over E,X: If the dial fails: RST to the app (fail closed), error code to Logs/UI
